            <ArticleTitle>Current guidelines for the evaluation and management of atopic dermatitis: A comparison of the Joint Task Force Practice Parameter and American Academy of Dermatology guidelines.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S49-S57</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0091-6749(17)30149-5</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jaci.2017.01.009</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Atopic dermatitis (AD) is a chronic pruritic inflammatory disease that commonly presents in the pediatric population. Although definitions and diagnosis of AD have largely been agreed upon, allergists and dermatologists have similar and divergent approaches to the management of AD. This review facilitated integration of the American Academy of Allergy, Asthma &amp; Immunology/American College of Allergy, Asthma &amp; Immunology Joint Task Force 2012 AD Practice Parameter and the 2014 American Academy of Dermatology guidelines to highlight the basic principles of AD management and discuss therapies and management of AD from the distinct perspectives of the allergist and dermatologist.</AbstractText>
